Several cited numbers come from the earlier version of oomuzrnk (df851ffe), not the final 962225ba:
- the 'Stack plus fix' drv paths (count-staged cdwgx714 clean, 0szmlh1x without the fix);
- the four adapter package paths (gyc6dg38, d1v2yghn, kxwd9jh5, kvs58cw0);
- the smoke report.
Their suite.json files and the smoke report still carry the old reason text ('one sealed qualification sample…'), so the final reason was never rendered.
My reproduction at 962225ba merged with 4778e6a1 gave count-staged drv 4yl5xgvk in all three cases: clean, with 40 stray .pyc files, and from git+file rev 773d7ddb (the merge) and rev 962225ba. Without the fix plus bytecode, it gave 1g43wj64. The packages against 75b6c7a8 are count k1nxnqjx, materialized 3c0pbh3l, lazy qadihhyk and eager fll11qja. Their driver binaries are identical to the lane's (lwlifqkq, s1wj1my8, c7k6bfw1), so the conclusions hold.

9540f5bb is not an ancestor of 75b6c7a8; both branch from 8cb80dfd. The full-public adapter depends on feynkit-generator, feynkit-graph and feynkit-model, which pull in idenso, spenso, linnest and others. Within that closure, the tree diff also touches:
- idenso: tensor/inference.rs, slot_contraction*, representations.rs, color/simplify.rs and the simplification files;
- spenso: network/library/symbolic.rs;
- linnest: label_placement.rs and ec_seed;
- feynkit-graph: dot.rs;
- symbolica-data: lib.rs.
The 'no signature changes' claim does hold: across these crates the only pub-item change is a removed pub(crate) fn factor_heads.

